t-response\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/incident-response\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"Incident Response\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/grc-compliance\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/grc-compliance\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"GRC & Compliance\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/vciso\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/vciso\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"vCISO\"}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Software Development\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"foot__col-heading\",\"children\":\"Software Development\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"foot__list\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/custom-software\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/custom-software\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"Custom Software\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/web-application-development\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/web-application-development\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"Web Applications\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/platform-engineering\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/platform-engineering\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"Platform & DevOps\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/erp\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/erp\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"ERP\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/crm\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/crm\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"CRM\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/hrm\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/hrm\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"HRM\"}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/lms\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/services/lms\",\"className\":\"foot__link\",\"children\":\"LMS\"}]}],\"$L26\"]}]]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]]}],\"$L29\",\"$L2a\"]}]}]\n2b:T1128,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"CollectionPage\",\"@id\":\"https://envenox.com/services#collection\",\"name\":\"Services\",\"description\":\"Envenox is a software development firm. We ship production systems — custom software, web applications, ERP and the platforms underneath them — and we keep an offensive security practice on staff that attacks what we build before anyone else gets the chance.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://envenox.com/#website\"},\"about\":{\"@id\":\"https://envenox.com/#organization\"},\"mainEntity\":{\"@type\":\"ItemList\",\"numberOfItems\":18,\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Penetration Testing\",\"description\":\"Manual, evidence-led testing with criticals reported the hour they are confirmed.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/penetration-testing\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Application Security\",\"description\":\"Secure code review, CI gates and threat models that engineers will actually maintain.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/application-security\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Cloud Security\",\"description\":\"Identity-path analysis across AWS, Azure and GCP, not a CSPM findings dump.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/cloud-security\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":4,\"name\":\"GRC & Compliance\",\"description\":\"SOC 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, DORA and NIS2, evidenced from systems you already run.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/grc-compliance\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":5,\"name\":\"Managed Detection & Response\",\"description\":\"24/7 detection and response on your telemetry, with detections written for your architecture.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/managed-detection-response\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":6,\"name\":\"Incident Response\",\"description\":\"24/7 hotline answered by a responder. Retainer or emergency.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/incident-response\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":7,\"name\":\"Red Teaming\",\"description\":\"Objective-based adversary simulation, with a purple-team debrief that transfers the knowledge.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/red-teaming\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":8,\"name\":\"vCISO\",\"description\":\"Fractional security leadership, with an explicit plan to make itself redundant.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/vciso\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":9,\"name\":\"Custom Software\",\"description\":\"Production systems with authorisation, audit and secrets handled properly from the first commit.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/custom-software\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":10,\"name\":\"Web Application Development\",\"description\":\"Server-rendered, budget-enforced front ends that work before JavaScript arrives.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/web-application-development\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":11,\"name\":\"Platform & DevOps\",\"description\":\"Reproducible infrastructure, short-lived pipeline identity, and a rehearsed rollback.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/platform-engineering\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":12,\"name\":\"ERP\",\"description\":\"Finance, inventory and procurement modelled on your exceptions, with history reconciled.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/erp\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":13,\"name\":\"CRM\",\"description\":\"Pipeline, activity and forecasting designed so sellers get something back from every field.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/crm\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":14,\"name\":\"HRM\",\"description\":\"Field-level access control, read-auditing, and joiner-mover-leaver flows that complete.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/hrm\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":15,\"name\":\"LMS\",\"description\":\"Audit-grade completion evidence with content people finish inside the window.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/lms\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":16,\"name\":\"QA & Test Automation\",\"description\":\"Deterministic end-to-end suites with a flake budget and a quarantine process.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/qa-automation\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":17,\"name\":\"Secure SDLC\",\"description\":\"One firm, two practices, one backlog. The seam between build and break, removed.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/devsecops\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":18,\"name\":\"Engagement Models\",\"description\":\"Projects, programmes, retainers and embedded teams — and which of them you do not need.\",\"url\":\"https://envenox.com/services/engagement-models\"}]}}13:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2b\"}}]\n14:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Envenox\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://envenox.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Services\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://envenox.com/services\\\"}]}\"}}]\n2c:Tdb3,\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  text-align: center;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  /* ONLY colour transitions. A transform here would break the house rule. */\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.btn:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg-hover);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border-hover);\n  /* Falls back to the resting label colour, so no existing variant changes.\n     A variant whose hover fill moves far in lightness needs to move its label\n     too, or the hover state quietly fails contrast while the resting state\n     passes — which is the kind of thing an audit on static screenshots misses. */\n  color: var(--btn-fg-hover, var(--btn-fg));\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true'],\n.btn:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.45;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true']:hover,\n.btn:disabled:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border);\n}\n\n/* ---- sizes. md and lg clear the 44x44 touch target. ---- */\n.btn--sm { min-height: 32px; padding-inline: var(--s3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--md { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--lg { min-height: 52px; min-width: 52px; padding-inline: var(--s6); font-size: var(--text-base); }\n\n.btn--full { width: 100%; }\n\n/* ---- variants ---- */\n.btn--primary {\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent);\n  --btn-fg: var(--accent-fg);\n  --btn-bg-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent);\n  --btn-border-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n.theme-light .btn--primary {\n  /* On paper, --accent is the DARK copper (#A04F1A) because it has to pass\n     4.5:1 as link TEXT. As a large filled surface that same value reads muddy\n     brown, which is not what the brand is. A fill has a different contrast\n     problem from text: the requirement is on the LABEL against the fill, and\n     ink on vibrant copper measures 6.9:1 — comfortably clear. So the fill gets\n     the real brand copper and the label goes dark. Links and the focus ring\n     keep --accent and stay legible. */\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-fg: var(--ink-900);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--accent-600);\n  --btn-fg-hover: var(--paper-50);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--accent-600);\n}\n.btn--secondary {\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--fg);\n}\n.btn--ghost {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--border);\n}\n.btn--ghost:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n.btn--danger-quiet {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--muted-strong);\n}\n.btn--danger-quiet:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.btn__icon { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }\n15:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-dark transition-theme u-section grain\",\"data-theme-section\":\"dark\",\"style\":{\"paddingTop\":\"calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s16))\"},\"aria-labelledby\":\"services-h1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow sv-hero__eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Services\"}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"id\":\"services-h1\",\"className\":\"sv-h1 sv-h1--long\",\"children\":\"Cybersecurity and Software Development\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-sub\",\"children\":\"Envenox is a software development firm. We ship production systems — custom software, web applications, ERP and the platforms underneath them — and we keep an offensive security practice on staff that attacks what we build before anyone else gets the chance.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-lede\",\"children\":\"Projects, programmes, retainers and embedded teams — and which of them you do not need.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-hero__actions\",\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-button\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$2c\"}],\"$L2d\"],\"$L2e\"]}],\"$L2f\"]}]}]]\n16:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-jump theme-deep\",\"aria-label\":\"Jump to a section of this page\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container sv-jump__inner\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",\"#cybersecurity\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#cybersecurity\",\"children\":\"Cybersecurity\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"#secure-sdlc\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#secure-sdlc\",\"children\":\"Secure SDLC\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"#software-engineering\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#software-engineering\",\"children\":\"Software Development\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"#engagement-models\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#engagement-models\",\"children\":\"Engagement Models\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"#proof\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#proof\",\"children\":\"Proof\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"#faq\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#faq\",\"children\":\"Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",\"#enquiry-form\",{\"className\":\"sv-jump__link\",\"href\":\"#enquiry-form\",\"children\":\"Start a conversation\"}]]}]}]\n30:T43d,\n.card {\n  position: relative;\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  color: inherit;\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.card--pad { padding: var(--s6); }\n.card--pad-lg { padding: var(--s8); }\n.card--flush { background-color: transparent; }\n\n/* Hover: colour only. Anything that moves the card is a spec violation. */\n.card[data-interactive='true']:hover,\n.card:has(.card__link):hover,\n.card:has(.card__link:focus-visible) {\n  background-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--surface) 88%, var(--fg) 12%);\n  border-color: var(--border-strong);\n}\n\n/* The stretched link. The anchor's own text stays the accessible name. */\n.card__link {\n  color: inherit;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  outline-offset: 4px;\n}\n.card__link::after {\n  content: '';\n  position: absolute;\n  inset: 0;\n  border-radius: inherit;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n/* Anything that must stay clickable inside a stretched-link card. */\n.card__above { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\n31:T859,\n.badge {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--badge-border, var(--border));\n  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n  background-color: var(--badge-bg, transparent);\n  color: var(--badge-fg, var(--muted-strong));\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: 0.04em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  padding: var(--s1) var(--s2);\n  /* normal + balance, NOT nowrap. Three separate pages overflowed 320px because\n     a badge held arbitrary data — \"3 weeks review, 14 weeks remediation\",\n     \"AWS Solutions Architect Professional\", a credibility sentence — and an\n     unbreakable chip wider than its card pushes the whole grid track past the\n     viewport. A badge is a label primitive, but callers legitimately put\n     variable-length data in one, and the component should survive that rather\n     than require every caller to override it. Severity badges keep nowrap\n     below: \"Critical\" is two syllables and must never break. */\n  white-space: normal;\n  text-wrap: balance;\n}\n.badge--severity {\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n.badge--sm { font-size: var(--text-xs); padding: 2px var(--s2); }\n.badge--md { padding: var(--s1) var(--s3); }\n\n.badge--neutral {\n  --badge-bg: var(--surface);\n  --badge-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --badge-border: var(--border);\n}\n.badge--brand {\n  --badge-bg: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 12%, transparent);\n  --badge-fg: var(--accent);\n  --badge-border: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 38%, transparent);\n}\n\n/* --- the only --signal-* usage in the codebase --- */\n.badge--severity {\n  --badge-bg: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sig) 14%, transparent);\n  --badge-fg: var(--sig);\n  --badge-border: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sig) 42%, transparent);\n  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n}\n.badge--severity .badge__dot {\n  width: 6px;\n  height: 6px;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  background-color: var(--sig);\n  flex: none;\n}\n.badge--critical { --sig: var(--signal-critical); }\n.badge--high { --sig: var(--signal-high); }\n.badge--medium { --sig: var(--signal-medium); }\n.badge--low { --sig: var(--signal-low); }\n.badge--info { --sig: var(--signal-info); }\n17:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-deep transition-theme u-section\",\"data-theme-section\":\"deep\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"pillars-h2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head__rule\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\",\"children\":\"How the work divides\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"pillars-h2\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"children\":\"Two pillars, and the seam between them\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head__lede\",\"children\":\"Threat models shape the build. The build get